00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:55.000
That's insane.

00:43:55.000 --> 00:44:00.000
That's like going against centuries of the common law and the most basic fundamental thing about our criminal justice system.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:06.000
My attorney jumped up and said, Your Honor, are you saying that a person can accidentally commit espionage?

00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:09.000
And she said, that's exactly what I'm saying.

00:44:09.000 --> 00:44:14.000
And she looked at me and she said, Mr. Kiriaku, you either did it or you didn't do it.

00:44:14.000 --> 00:44:16.000
And I think you did it.

00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:19.000
That's what she said in a hearing.

00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:23.000
I knew I had literally no chance.

00:44:23.000 --> 00:44:29.000
In fact, we were walking out of the courtroom and I said to the lead attorney who was a legend,

00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:33.000
Plato Kacheris, legendary figure in Washington law.

00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:34.000
